      "sourceTextSha256": "991973b06d9d7436a106fa61263693065e20c555bdcabad134ffda5cb411fe04",
      "text": "Day 12 · Breakfast, then the lagoons of Honda, Ch’iar Khota, Hedionda and Cañapa, the Ollagüe volcano viewpoint and the Chiguana salt flat, before reaching the Salar de Uyuni, the largest salt flat on Earth, about 10,500 km² at 3,650 m: in the rainy season, a thin layer of water turns it into the world’s largest mirror. See salt extraction at Colchani, the Ojos del Salar and Fish Island with its giant cacti. Box lunch included. Overnight in Uyuni.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1p43mEGxeh35l0VLkcj1IlUV9E-hKpInp",
